{"book":10,"chapter":31,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / ASYNCHRONY / CHAPTER 31","slides":[{"title":"By hand","sub":"Chapter 31 · How async works","short":"Intro","main":"Our own futures, waker, executor: std only.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["By hand","std only","No magic"],"captions":["Our own futures, waker, executor and timer, so async and await stop being magic","It all lives in std::future and std::task: one trait, two types and a few helpers","async and await are state-machine mechanics"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Future","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Waker","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"block_on","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Timer","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"std::future","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"std::task","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":34.0,"text":"async = state machine","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.4,28.0]}]},{"title":"Future and Poll","sub":"Trait","short":"Future","main":"poll returns Ready or Pending and never blocks.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["trait Future","Poll","Never blocks"],"captions":["fn poll(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Self::Output>","Poll::Ready(T): done; Poll::Pending: not yet, come back later","The executor calls poll and it never blocks: either the value is there, or Pending"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["trait Future {","    type Output;","    fn poll(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context) -> Poll<Self::Output>;","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":7.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Ready(5)","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Pending","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"executor","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"poll()","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.1,28.3]}]},{"title":"Pending and wake","sub":"Contract","short":"Pending","main":"Before Pending, arrange a future wake.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Pending → wait","wake()","Forgotten wake"],"captions":["A future returned Pending: the executor stops polling it until it gets a signal","The signal is a waker.wake() call: from the OS, another thread, a timer or the future itself (wake_by_ref before Pending)","Pending with no future wake: the task hangs forever, silently"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Pending → wait queue","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["cx.waker().wake_by_ref();","Poll::Pending"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Pending without wake ✕ hang","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[16.7,25.5]}]},{"title":"Waker","sub":"Task handle","short":"Waker","main":"Cloneable; Wake for Arc; noop for tests.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Task handle","Wake for Arc","noop"],"captions":["A Waker is cloned, sent to another thread and called; inside: a pointer and a table of four functions","Simpler than RawWaker: impl Wake for Task { fn wake(self: Arc<Self>) } and Waker::from(arc)","Waker::noop() is a dummy waker for tests, when you poll the future in a loop yourself"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"clone","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"wake","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"wake_by_ref","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"drop","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl Wake for Task {","    fn wake(self: Arc<Self>) { /* into the queue */ }","}","let w = Waker::from(task_arc);"],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let mut cx = Context::from_waker(Waker::noop());"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[17.1,32.8]}]},{"title":"Simple futures","sub":"Ready, Yield, CountDown","short":"Simple","main":"A struct with one field and poll.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Ready","YieldOnce","CountDown"],"captions":["Ready<T>: on the first poll takes the value out of the Option and returns Ready","YieldOnce: first poll is wake_by_ref and Pending, second is Ready(()): like handing control back","CountDown: counts polls; the compiler turns async code into structs just like these"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct Ready<T>(Option<T>);","fn poll(..) -> Poll<T> {","    Poll::Ready(self.0.take().unwrap())","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["if self.done { Poll::Ready(()) } else {","    self.done = true;","    cx.waker().wake_by_ref();","    Poll::Pending","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"go","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[8.2,27.6]}]},{"title":"block_on","sub":"Loop and park","short":"block_on","main":"Poll in a loop, park/unpark, spurious wakeups.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Loop it","park and unpark","Spurious wakeups"],"captions":["Simple block_on: poll in a loop with a noop waker: works, but burns CPU","Better: the waker wakes the thread via thread::unpark, and after Pending the loop calls thread::park","park may return without a wake: just poll again, it is harmless"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["loop {","    match fut.as_mut().poll(&mut cx) {","        Poll::Ready(v) => return v,","        Poll::Pending => {}","    }","}"],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"poll → Pending\npark()","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"wake()\nunpark()","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":240.0,"h":34.0,"text":"wakeup ≠ ready","tone":"yellow","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.6,27.2]}]},{"title":"Timer","sub":"Thread and flag","short":"Timer","main":"Shared state and a fresh waker.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Timer thread","Shared state","New waker"],"captions":["Delay starts a thread on the first poll: sleep, set the flag, call wake","Flag and waker sit in Arc<Mutex<…>>: the race \"event came before the waker was saved\" is impossible","On every poll save the freshest waker: the task may have moved to another executor"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"thread: sleep(d)","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"flag + wake()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["struct Shared { done: bool, waker: Option<Waker> }","state: Arc<Mutex<Shared>>"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["s.waker = Some(cx.waker().clone());","Poll::Pending"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.2,28.5]}]},{"title":"Combinators","sub":"Map, Join, Select","short":"Combinators","main":"Polling nested futures.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Map","Join","Select"],"captions":["Map: polls the inner future and applies a function to the result","Join: holds two futures and two results, polls both until it has both, like gather","Select: returns the first one ready; future fields need a Pin projection (pin-project) or Box::pin"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Future<A>","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Future<B>","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"text":"map(f)","size":11.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"A: Ready(1)","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"B: Pending","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":108.0,"text":"Join → Pending","size":11.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"A: Pending","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"B: Ready(2)","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":108.0,"text":"Select → Ready(B)","size":11.0}]],"cues":[16.7,28.1]}]},{"title":"Executor","sub":"Task queue","short":"Executor","main":"Task, queue, wake puts the task back.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Task and queue","wake → queue","Loop"],"captions":["A task is Arc<Task> with Mutex<Option<Pin<Box<dyn Future>>>>; spawn puts it in the queue (a channel)","When called, the waker puts the task back into the channel: that is how a task wakes up","Loop: take a task, make a waker, poll; Ready: drop it; Pending: wait for wake; empty: exit"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":80.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":34.0,"text":"task 1","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":34.0,"text":"task 2","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":280.0,"y":60.0,"w":80.0,"h":34.0,"text":"task 3","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"q","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"ready queue","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"wake()","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"to queue","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["while let Ok(task) = queue.recv() {","    // poll(task); Pending → wait for wake","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.4,27.0]}]},{"title":"State machine","sub":"What async turns into","short":"State machine","main":"States, transitions, size.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["States","Transitions","size_of_val"],"captions":["async fn with two .await becomes an enum: Start, WaitFirst, WaitSecond, Done; each holds only the variables needed later","poll: match on the state; inner poll Pending: stay; Ready: go to the next","A future's size is its largest state: check it with size_of_val(&async_block)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Start","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Wait1","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Wait2","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Done","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Wait1","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":110.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":170.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":210.0,"y":66.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Wait2","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"Ready → next","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let f = async { let big = [0u8; 100]; tick().await; big.len() };","println!(\"{}\", size_of_val(&f));"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":8.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.9,30.5]}]},{"title":"Pitfalls","sub":"Common mistakes","short":"Pitfalls","main":"Pending without wake, poll after Ready, blocking.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Pending without wake","Poll after Ready","Blocking in poll"],"captions":["A hang: returned Pending and forgot to arrange a wake","Poll after Ready is undefined behavior, may panic: wrap in Fuse","A blocking call inside poll freezes the executor; lost and stale wakers; flag/waker race: use a mutex"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Pending, no wake ✕","tone":"red","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Ready → poll again ✕","tone":"red","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":230.0,"h":34.0,"text":"sleep() in poll ✕",